te** \u2014 no change-manager approval was needed since v5.0.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** Opened **SEV2 incident INC-0001** (\"payments-api elevated error rate after v5.1.0 deploy; rolled back to v5.0.0\"), and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\nFollow-up for the humans: the v5.1.0 regression still needs root-causing before that version is re-attempted in production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "Need to find payments service deployments to identify most recent healthy version. Let me list deployments.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a13c44f44074938afd256e", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a13c44f44074938afd2573", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The service name \"payments\" wasn't recognized. Let me probe a few likely service identifiers.", "reasoning_content": "Service \"payments\" unknown. Maybe service names differ. Try get_service_status with variations? We don't have a list-services tool. Could ask human. Maybe try \"payment-service\"? Let's try a couple guesses... but tools can have side effects; get_service_status is read-only, fine to probe.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a13c44fb057ad1a1e6161b", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a13c44fb057ad1a1e6162e", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "t